## Why This Is Asked

Adds a practical multi-tenant privacy control layer to a beginner API, highlighting data isolation, per-tenant budgets, and simple governance in a real system.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-tenancy isolation
- Per-tenant privacy budgets (epsilon, delta)
- Header validation (X-tenant-id)
- Tenant-scoped configuration
- Observability and audits

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: tenant-aware config lookup (Express)
function tenantMiddleware(req, res, next) {
  const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant-id'];
  if (!tenant) return res.status(400).send('Missing X-tenant-id');
  req.tenant = loadTenantConfig(tenant); // returns {epsilon, delta, ...}
  if (!req.tenant) return res.status(403).send('Unknown tenant');
  next();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test for cross-tenant data leakage?
- How would you migrate tenants to per-tenant budgets with zero downtime?

## Why This Is Asked
This angle tests practical edge compute handling: budget-aware routing, deterministic fallbacks, and testability in real apps.

## Key Concepts
- Budget-aware orchestration: enforce per-request time budgets for compute paths
- Deterministic fallback: seed heuristic with user_id_masked and client_timestamp for reproducibility
- Telemetry: track latency, fallback usage, and model_version for auditing
- Testability: budget-bound tests, fairness across devices, end-to-end reproducibility

## Code Example
```javascript
function selectScore(input){
  const {budgetMs, start}=input;
  const canRunModel = simulateModelCost(input) <= budgetMs;
  if(!canRunModel){
    return heuristicScore(input.user_id_masked, input.client_timestamp);
  }
  return modelScore(input);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you ensure reproducibility if the heuristic depends on timestamps with clock drift?
- How would you expand this to multi-tenant environments with fair queueing?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates API design skills, robust aggregation under adversarial inputs, and tamper-evident provenance in a privacy-preserving setting.

## Key Concepts
- Privacy-preserving aggregation with robustness to compromised devices
- Append-only ledger with Merkle proofs for auditability
- Replay protection and device churn handling

## Code Example
```javascript
// Data types for CCA score shares
